1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,809
Standby: if this person is out, what stalls?

2
00:00:03,809 --> 00:00:08,351
Pick any real teammate on the site and the days they will be away

3
00:00:08,351 --> 00:00:13,400
Standby reads their Jira issues, Confluence pages and Teamwork Graph, as you

4
00:00:13,400 --> 00:00:17,817
Every item lands on a ring: red means nobody else is on record, amber one other person, green covered

5
00:00:17,817 --> 00:00:23,364
Hover any node to see the work behind it

6
00:00:23,364 --> 00:00:27,046
Backups come from people who already work in the same projects, spaces and teams

7
00:00:27,046 --> 00:00:29,706
Click a count to focus on what stalls

8
00:00:29,706 --> 00:00:35,557
Each card says why it is urgent and who can pick it up

9
00:00:35,557 --> 00:00:40,636
Reassigning is opt-in per issue, and nothing changes without a confirmation

10
00:00:40,636 --> 00:00:45,259
Each source reports its own status, so a gap is never silent

11
00:00:45,259 --> 00:00:54,499
One confirmation drafts the handover page in Confluence

12
00:00:54,499 --> 00:01:11,207
The draft lists every item with its suggested backup, ready to edit and publish

13
00:01:11,207 --> 00:01:14,849
Standby: a bus-factor fire drill for Jira and Confluence
